---
description: "Apply marketplace payment, commission, refund, and payout safety rules when implementing Laravel financial workflows or payment-provider integrations."
---

# Payment and Marketplace Rules

- Payment provider integration MUST be abstracted behind an application interface.
- Provider webhooks MUST be authenticated/verified according to the provider documentation.
- Never trust client-submitted payment status.
- Payment status changes MUST be driven by trusted backend/provider events.
- Persist immutable transaction references and snapshots.
- Monetary values MUST use precise decimal-safe representations.
- Commission rules must be configuration-driven but snapshotted onto the transaction at the time of contracting.
- Refunds MUST reference the original payment transaction.
- Payout/release to the driver MUST require the documented delivery completion condition.
- Webhook processing MUST be idempotent.
- Never log card data, security codes, access tokens, or payment secrets.
- Keep provider-specific models/adapters isolated so the provider can be replaced.
- Financial operations must create audit events.
